- Fetch attempts and source snapshots.
- Evidence claims and historical claim versions.
- Admission requirements and eligibility restrictions.
- Funding packages and conditions.
- Eligibility results and ranking explanations.
- Research runs, queued jobs, attempts, and leases.
- Parser health and provider usage.
- Change events and audit logs.
- Saved opportunities and application tracking.
- Tasks and document checklists.
- In-app notifications and email delivery records.
- System health and scheduler status.

Use UUIDs, foreign keys, appropriate indexes, unique constraints, timestamps, and transactional updates.

Prevent duplicate records through stable source identities and normalized URLs. Preserve historical evidence rather than silently replacing previous observations.

Separate shared research data from user-owned information.

Implement authorization and database access controls so users cannot access or modify other users' profiles, saved opportunities, notes, tasks, or notifications.

