### 16. Free-Tier-First Resource Management

Optimize for sustainable operation within free-tier limits.

Implement caching, conditional requests, incremental crawling, URL deduplication, content hashes, bounded concurrency, and priority-based scheduling.

Measure actual request volume, database usage, execution duration, queue depth, provider quota consumption, and failure rates.

When a quota is exhausted:

1. Record the failure.
2. Preserve existing data and evidence.
3. Prioritize important open opportunities.
4. Resume remaining jobs when capacity becomes available.
5. Mark the system Degraded if coverage is materially affected.

Do not silently stop searching or label a partial run as a comprehensive search.

Document which capabilities depend on optional paid infrastructure, even though those services remain disabled by default.

